Chapter: BoundedSigRuntime

 Bounded signatures, stage B: the runtime boundary guards do not
 false-trap on in-range values. inc-byte's bounded parameter is
 range-checked at the callee entry (Eiffel-style precondition) and 5
 passes; clamp-ret's bounded return is range-checked before the
 epilogue (postcondition) and 9 passes. Both guards are emitted (the
 param guard unconditionally; the return guard because __narrow n is
 not statically provable in range - the __narrow takes lint
 responsibility now that CDX2051 is an error, and the emit-side
 guard still runs) and both are exercised here.

Section: Definitions

  inc-byte : Integer between 0 and 255 -> Integer
  inc-byte (n) = n + 1

  clamp-ret : Integer -> Integer between 0 and 15
  clamp-ret (n) = __narrow n

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (inc-byte 5))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (clamp-ret 9))
  end
